🚀 Day 1 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 33 – Search in Rotated Sorted Array.

This problem helped me strengthen my understanding of Binary Search and how it can be modified to work efficiently even on a rotated sorted array.

💡 Approach: Binary Search (O(log n))

Instead of performing a linear search, I used a modified Binary Search. At every step, I identified which half of the array was sorted. Based on the target's range, I discarded the irrelevant half and continued searching in the remaining portion. This reduced the time complexity from O(n) to O(log n).

📚 Key Learnings:
✅ Understanding Binary Search beyond a normally sorted array
✅ Identifying the sorted half in a rotated array
✅ Applying conditional logic to eliminate half of the search space
✅ Improving problem-solving and algorithmic thinking
✅ Writing optimized solutions with O(log n) complexity

Every problem solved is one step closer to becoming a better software engineer. Looking forward to learning something new every day! 🚀

